WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.800
A design token is a named
design decision: a colour,

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:06.940
a spacing step, a radius, a duration.

00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:12.270
Tokens let designers and engineers refer
to the same decision by the same name,

00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:15.600
so changing it in one place
changes it everywhere.

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:18.860
You will audit what is
actually in the code,

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:23.840
collapse near-duplicates into primitives,
and point a card at those names.

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:28.140
Before naming anything, find
out what is actually in use.

00:00:28.430 --> 00:00:33.390
A quick search of a stylesheet or component
folder for hex codes and pixel values is

00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:39.100
usually revealing. It is common to find
a dozen greys where three were intended,

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:46.040
and borders in #E4E4E4, #E5E5E5,

00:00:46.170 --> 00:00:51.000
and #E6E6E6 that nobody can tell apart.

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:56.020
Each near-duplicate is a decision
someone made without a shared reference.

00:00:56.540 --> 00:01:00.380
Primitive tokens describe raw
values with neutral names.

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:02.820
They form your palette and scales.

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:06.680
Map every audited value
to its nearest primitive.

00:01:07.070 --> 00:01:12.060
The three almost-identical
borders all become neutral-200.

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:17.400
If a value has no sensible home, ask
whether it is a real need or an accident.

00:01:17.950 --> 00:01:22.560
The card looks almost identical,
but now it moves with the system.

00:01:22.910 --> 00:01:28.700
Change radius-2 and every card,
input, and menu that uses it follows.

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:34.280
The 7 pixel radius and the 15 pixel
padding were not a different design.

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:37.840
They were drift. They map to 8 and 16.

00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:42.860
Teams often keep tokens in a
JSON file and generate CSS,

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:47.080
Tailwind configuration, and
design-tool variables from it.

00:01:47.390 --> 00:01:51.500
That is worth doing once more than
one platform consumes the tokens.

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:57.940
For a single web app, CSS custom properties
in one file are a fine source of truth.

00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:01.780
Audit what is in use before
you design a token set.

00:02:02.090 --> 00:02:04.720
Primitive tokens name raw values.

00:02:04.910 --> 00:02:07.400
Map every existing value to one.

00:02:07.730 --> 00:02:12.760
Keep a single source of truth, and generate
other formats only when you need them.

00:02:13.050 --> 00:02:16.260
Next, primitives tell you what a value is.

00:02:16.510 --> 00:02:21.540
Semantic tokens tell you what it is for,
which is what makes a theme possible.
